Subject: let a container reach the host's systemd-resolved stub

A container's /etc/resolv.conf is copied from the host. On hosts that run
systemd-resolved (Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, GitHub's runners) it names
127.0.0.53, and --net-ip (patch 0009) redirected every connect/sendto to a
loopback address to the container's own address, so on a user-defined
network every DNS lookup timed out ("connection timed out; no servers could
be reached"; found by the compatibility suite in CI).

connect() and sendto() to exactly 127.0.0.53 and 127.0.0.54 are now left
alone, so the query reaches the host's resolver. Nothing is redirected to
any other server, public or not; a container's own service on those two
addresses is the only case that changes. Phones have no such stub: Android
containers use the resolver file the app writes.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92), after patches 0001-0014

diff --git a/src/extension/net_ip/net_ip.c b/src/extension/net_ip/net_ip.c
index 425369d..4fb9436 100644
--- a/src/extension/net_ip/net_ip.c
+++ b/src/extension/net_ip/net_ip.c
@@ -122,6 +122,13 @@ static bool rewrite4(uint32_t own, bool is_bind, uint32_t *addr, uint16_t *port)
 		*addr = LOOPBACK;
 		return true;
 	}
+	/* The host's own systemd-resolved stub addresses (127.0.0.53 and
+	 * 127.0.0.54): a container's resolv.conf copied from such a host names
+	 * one, and it is the host's resolver, not the container's loopback.
+	 * Left alone, the query reaches the resolver the host is configured
+	 * with; nothing is sent to any other server.  */
+	if (a == 0x7f000035 || a == 0x7f000036)
+		return false;
 	if ((a & NET_MASK) == NET_BASE) {
 		*port = shift_port(p);
 		return *port != p;
